 2. 🎬 Bessent doubles down: &quot;I am the house&quot; 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Photo: JaMar Jones for Axios During our interview Friday for "The Axios Show," I asked Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent if he regretted his boast last month: "I am the house now" — challenging markets, which rebuked him , to bet against his "asymmetric information" at their peril. 

 "No," replied Bessent, an investment manager for four decades. "The house doesn't win every hand. The house plays percentages. … Did I maybe hurt some fragile egos on Wall Street? … If you have an ego, you lose a lot of money." "Everyone in the market knows you don't win every hand, but you win over time," he added. "What I meant by 'I am the house' is that I have superior information." Watch the episode . 



 
 
