 5. 🎓 Cornell president vows to reshape campus practices 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 People gather prior to a hearing on sexual assault on campus at Cornell University in Ithaca, N.Y., Thursday, Oct. 1, 2026. (AP Photo/Matt Rourke) In an eight-minute video message to the Cornell community, President Michael Kotlikoff described the past week as "one of the most difficult weeks in our history" and pledged to be "more transparent" about the school's handling of the alleged gang rape of a student at a fraternity house in 2024. 

 The president promised Cornell will produce "research that can deepen our understanding of sexual assault, trauma, intoxication and consent, and help shape better practices and policies elsewhere," including a deep look at the Greek system. "This is a defining moment in Cornell's history," Kotlikoff concluded. "We owe it to Jane Doe and to survivors of assault to get this right." Watch the video … Get the latest . 

 
 
