 7. 🤖 AI fears sink in 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Quinnipiac . Chart: Neal Rothschild/Axios 73% of Americans say they're concerned that AI advances threaten human survival, a new Quinnipiac poll finds.

 Why it matters: Forecasts of cataclysmic AI doom scenarios are sinking into the national psyche. By the numbers: 34% say AI will do more good than harm in their day-to-day life. 53% say more harm than good, with the rest not giving an opinion.

 24% say they have "a lot" or "some" trust in the leaders of AI companies. 74% don't trust AI leaders. Explore the results ... Methodology . 

 
 
